-- title:
--   Node coordinates at a supersingular crossing from a chart presentation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$, and fix a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak X$ of level $p$, that is a term `𝔛 : DRModelPackage p` consisting of the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of $X_0(p)$ over $\mathbb Z$ together with its properness, flatness, integrality and normality data, generic-fibre curve models $M_0$ over $\mathbb Q$ and $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ identified with the corresponding base changes, the Galois and compatibility laws relating them, the two cuspidal sections, the smooth locus, and the remaining components of that structure.
--
--   The following groups of data and hypotheses are assumed.
--
--   Chart reading on the generic fibre: a nonemptiness condition for the preimage of the finite chart, and the hypothesis `hMη`, which requires that for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ℤ ↥(modularFunctionFieldFull p) (IgusaScheme.jFull p)` the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar p` obtained by taking the germ of $a$ along $\mathfrak X.e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, passing to the function field of $M_\eta.C$ and transporting back by `𝔛.Mη.ffEquiv.symm`, coincides, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of $a$ regarded as a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$.
--
--   Comparison of place sets: a bijection `ePl` between the places of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-valued functions in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` and those in `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, together with `hePl_fun`: whenever $f$ and $f'$ in the two fields have the same underlying Laurent series, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $V$ if and only if $f'$ lies in that of `ePl V`, and $V.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f = (\mathrm{ePl}\,V).\mathrm{evalAt}\,f'$.
--
--   Specialization data in characteristic $p$: an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a ring homomorphism `red : A →+* k`, modular polynomial data `data` for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` (the bivariate reduction of `data.Φ` mod $p$ equals $(C X^p - X)(C X - X^p)$), integrality hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` for the Hecke maps $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$ at level $1$ and $p$, a place specialization `P : PlaceSpecialization A p 1 data hKr k red hα hβ`, a prolongation tuple `R : ProlongationTuple P`, the hypothesis `hqN : ¬ p ∣ 1`, and the hypothesis `hR : R.IsModel`, that is the conjunction of the two divisor laws and the cusp laws at $\infty$ and at $0$.
--
--   Supersingular places and their widths: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` with `hW` saying that $W$ is precisely `ssPlaces p 1 k`, the hypotheses `hreg : R.RegularityLaw W` and `hval : R.NodeValueLaw W`, a function $e$ on places with $1 \le e\,w$ for $w \in W$, and `hVI`, requiring `R.ValueIntegralityLaw w` for each $w \in W$ (every element of the node integers at $w$ has $V$-value in $A$ for all places $V$ above $w$).
--
--   The unramified base: a discrete valuation ring $O$ which is a domain, a ring isomorphism `eO` of $O$ with the intersection $A \cap K^{I}$, where $K^{I}$ is the fixed field of the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (formally, the comap of $A$ along the inclusion of that fixed field), the hypothesis `hϖO` that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$, a fraction field $K$ of $O$, a ring homomorphism `ιK : K →+* AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hιK` stating that on $O$ it agrees with `eO` followed by the inclusions $A \cap K^{I} \hookrightarrow K^{I} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the hypothesis `hιA` that $\iota_K$ maps $O$ into $A$, and a homomorphism `toκ : O →+* k` with `htoκ` stating that `toκ` is `red` applied to the image of `eO` under those inclusions.
--
--   The resolved model and the chosen crossing: a term `𝔛reg : DRResolvedModelPackage p 𝔛 O k toκ`, consisting of a scheme $Y$ over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ with a proper morphism `toDR` to $\mathfrak X_O := \mathfrak X \times_{\mathbb Z} \operatorname{Spec} O$ over the base, regularity and Krull-dimension bounds on the fibre over $p$, the isomorphism statements over the smooth locus and over the generic fibre, a finite type `node` of crossings with widths `width ≥ 1`, a bijection `nodeEquiv` of `node` with the fibre product of the two component maps $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$, a family `comp` of invertible ideal sheaf data indexed by `X0MqComponents width` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_n \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}\,n - 1)$, and the remaining clauses of that structure; a bijection `σN : ↥W ≃ 𝔛reg.node` with `hσN : 𝔛reg.width (σN w) = e w`; a place $w \in W$; and an orientation bit `swap : Bool`. Throughout, $x_w$ denotes the point of $\mathfrak X_O$ obtained from `𝔛reg.nodeEquiv (σN ⟨w, hw⟩)` by the first projection of the fibre product of the two component maps followed by `𝔛.compInf k` and `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`.
--
--   Branch matching `hswap`: for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` fixed by the arithmetic Galois action of every element of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, and every $O$-point $s$ of $\mathfrak X_O$ which is a section of the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ and whose composite with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring map $O \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ built from `eO` and the inclusions, followed by the first projection, is the generic-fibre point attached to `ePl V` by `𝔛.Mη.pointEquivPlace` composed with $\mathfrak X.e_\eta$ and the first projection: if `P.IsStrictFst V` holds (the Frobenius on geometric places carries `P.reduceFst V` to `P.reduceSnd V`, and the double Frobenius does not fix `P.reduceFst V`), then the image of the closed point of $O$ under $s$ lies in the range of the base map of `(if swap then 𝔛.compZero k else 𝔛.compInf k) ≫ DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` and not in the range of the other of the two; and symmetrically, if `P.IsStrictSnd V` holds, the closed point lies in the range associated with `if swap then 𔛛.compInf k else 𔛛.compZero k` and not in the other.
--
--   The function-field reading: integrality of $\mathfrak X_O$, a ring homomorphism `φ` from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, the hypothesis `hφO` that $\varphi$ carries the germ at $x_w$ of the global function determined by $a \in O$ (via the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$) to the image of $\iota_K(a)$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`, a nonemptiness condition for the preimage of the finite chart in $\mathfrak X_O$, and `hφj`: $\varphi$ reads the finite chart algebra coefficientwise, exactly as `hMη` does on the generic fibre.
--
--   Node matching `hnodePt`: for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` together with a proof that `P.reduceFst V ∈ W`, if $V$ is fixed by the inertia arithmetic Galois action and neither `P.IsStrictFst V` nor `P.IsStrictSnd V` holds, then every $O$-section $s$ of $\mathfrak X_O$ whose generic-fibre matching condition with `ePl V` is as in `hswap` sends the closed point of $O$ to the crossing point attached to `σN ⟨P.reduceFst V, _⟩`.
--
--   The $j$-value pin `hxj`: there exists $\hat\jmath \in O$ with `red ⟨ιK (algebraMap O K ĵ), _⟩` equal to $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,1)$, and an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at $x_w$ with $\varphi$ of the image of $t$ in the function field equal to `ProlongationTuple.jFun 1 p` minus the image of $\iota_K(\hat\jmath)$.
--
--   Specialization and local equation at the crossing: hypotheses `hspInf` and `hspZero` stating that the images of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under `𝔛.compInf k ≫ DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` and under `𝔛.compZero k ≫ DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` both specialize to $x_w$; elements $u$, $v$, $w_0$ of the stalk at $x_w$ with $w_0$ a unit (`hw₀`), with $u v = p^{\,\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(\sigma_N w)} w_0$ (`huv`), with $\operatorname{span}\{p, u, v\}$ the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hmax`), and with $\operatorname{span}\{p, u\}$, respectively $\operatorname{span}\{p, v\}$, equal to the comap along the specialization map of stalks for `hspInf`, respectively `hspZero`, of the maximal ideal of the corresponding stalk (`h𝔭inf`, `h𝔭zero`).
--
--   The chart presentation `hchartV`: for every $O$-point $t$ of `𝔛reg.Y` which is a section of `𝔛reg.toBase`, with $t \gg \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ sending the closed point of $O$ to $x_w$, and every $d : \mathbb N$ such that the additive valuation of $O$ of the image of $v$ under the induced map on stalks at the closed point equals $d$, and every component $c$ of `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`: the closed point of $t$ lies in the support of `𝔛reg.comp c` if and only if $c = \mathrm{chainPos}\,\mathrm{width}\,(\sigma_N w)\,d$, that is $c = \mathrm{inl}\,0$ when $d = 0$, $c = \mathrm{inr}\,(\sigma_N w, d-1)$ when $0 < d < \mathrm{width}(\sigma_N w)$, and $c = \mathrm{inl}\,1$ otherwise.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, there exist an intermediate field $K_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$, node coordinates $c_1 : R.\mathrm{NodeCoordinates}\,K_0\,w$ — that is a pair $x, y$ in the subring `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w` of node integers at $w$ whose Laurent series lie in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (1 * p) K₀`, with first node residue of $x$ zero and $\mathrm{ord} = 1$ for the second residue of $x$ at the arithmetic-Frobenius translate of $w$, and with second node residue of $y$ zero and $w.\mathrm{ord}$ of the first residue of $y$ equal to $1$ — and an element $u_0$ of `R.nodeIntegersOver K₀ w`, such that the following five assertions hold.
--
--   First, $u_0$ is a unit. Second, $c_1.x \cdot c_1.y = \mathrm{nodeConst}\,K_0\,w(p)^{\,\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(\sigma_N w)} \cdot u_0$, where `nodeConst` is the constant embedding of the coefficient subring $A \cap K_0$ into the node integers over $K_0$ and $p$ is taken as an element of that subring. Third, $\varphi$ of the image in the function field of `if swap then v else u` equals $c_1.x$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)`. Fourth, $\varphi$ of the image of `if swap then u else v` equals $c_1.y$.
--
--   Fifth, the depth dictionary: for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` with `P.reduceFst V = w` which is fixed by the arithmetic Galois action of every element of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, every $O$-point $t$ of `𝔛reg.Y` which is a section of `𝔛reg.toBase` and whose composite with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring map $O \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ determined by `eO` and the inclusions, followed by $t \gg \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ and the first projection, equals the generic-fibre point attached to `ePl V` by `𝔛.Mη.pointEquivPlace` composed with $\mathfrak X.e_\eta$ and the first projection, and every $d : \mathbb N$ with $c_1.\mathrm{yDepth}\,V = A.\mathrm{valuation}(p)^d$ (the $A$-valuation of $V.\mathrm{evalAt}(c_1.y)$), and every component $c$ of `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`: the closed point of $t$ lies in the support of `𝔛reg.comp c` if and only if
--   $$c = \mathrm{chainPos}\,\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}\,(\sigma_N w)\,\bigl(\text{if } \mathrm{swap} \text{ then } \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{width}(\sigma_N w) - d \text{ else } d\bigr).$$
--
--   This is the local dictionary at a supersingular crossing of $X_0(p)$: the local equation $uv = p^{e}$ times a unit at the crossing point of the Deligne–Rapoport model over the unramified base $O$ is transported through the function-field reading $\varphi$ into node coordinates over a number field, and the depth of the $y$-coordinate at a place above $w$ determines which component of the resolved special fibre an $O$-section meets. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts), where the crossing enumeration and the orientation bit are produced uniformly in the supersingular places.
